{
  "requirement": "When given `--path <crate-dir>` and no existing Habeas dev dependency, `habeas setup` MUST add that local crate as the dev dependency. Repeating setup MUST NOT add a duplicate Habeas dependency.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "**Verdict: the requirement is met.** The implementation is correct. The test is somewhat thin but sufficient.\n\n**Implementation** (`src/setup.rs`)\n- `has_habeas_dev_dependency` returns true when `[dev-dependencies]` has a `habeas` key. It reads the table through `as_table_like`, so both inline and `[dev-dependencies.habeas]` forms are covered. It is tagged `{impl}` for this requirement.\n- `run` calls that check, and only when no dependency exists it runs `cargo add --dev habeas --manifest-path <Cargo.toml>`.\n- When `--path` is given, `run` also passes `--path <canonicalized local crate>` to `cargo add`. This adds the local crate as the dev dependency, as the requirement states.\n- A second run finds the existing dependency and skips `cargo add`, so no duplicate is added. A TOML table cannot hold duplicate keys anyway.\n- A failing `cargo add` is reported as an error.\n\n**Tests** (`tests/setup.rs`, `tests/cli.rs`)\n- `setup_is_repeatable` is tagged `{test}` for this requirement. It builds a fixture project with no Habeas dependency. It runs `habeas setup --path $CARGO_MANIFEST_DIR` twice, and both runs must succeed. In `Cargo.toml` it then asserts that `[dev-dependencies]` exists, that `habeas` is present and that `path = ` is present. That last assertion would catch an implementation that ignored `--path`, because the run is offline.\n- Other setup tests (`tests/setup.rs` lines 114–204) and `tests/symposium_hook_smoke.py` also run `setup --path`. They exercise the same path through different scenarios. `tests/cli.rs` checks that invalid argument combinations are rejected.\n\n**Minor gaps**\n- No assertion counts the `habeas` entries in `Cargo.toml`.\n- No assertion checks that the recorded path equals the local crate.\n- No separate test starts with a pre-existing Habeas dev dependency. The second run of `setup_is_repeatable` covers that case.\n\nThese do not undermine the behaviour. I found no acknowledged FIXMEs.",
  "inputs": [
